   "reply": "I couldn't save the note to the project, so it isn't remembered yet. Writing `CLAUDE.md` in the project directory was denied by your permission settings. I haven't tried another location.\n\n**List output for an empty store:** nothing. I ran `python -m fieldnotes.cli list` with `NOTES_HOME` pointing at a fresh temp directory. It printed no output and exited with code 0. The `list` command only loops over stored notes, so an empty store gives no message at all.\n\n`NOTES_HOME` is unset in this shell, and `store.notes_path()` reads it directly. Running `list` without it set would raise a `KeyError`. A missing `notes.json` is treated as an empty list, which is why the empty-store case works.\n\nIf you want the note persisted, tell me where to put it or allow writes to `CLAUDE.md`. I can also make `list` print something like \"No notes.\" for an empty store.",
